1
00:00:31,786 --> 00:00:32,618
Do you like them, dear?

2
00:00:44,118 --> 00:00:45,049
Which pair do you like, Nava?

3
00:00:46,390 --> 00:00:47,270
Left or right?

4
00:00:48,456 --> 00:00:49,256
The left pair.

5
00:00:51,603 --> 00:00:53,353
Looks like she likes the left one more.

6
00:00:56,050 --> 00:00:56,429
Yes.

7
00:01:02,577 --> 00:01:03,750
Then I'll take this pair.

8
00:01:04,589 --> 00:01:05,333
Size 31, please.

9
00:01:05,358 --> 00:01:06,053
Sure.

10
00:01:11,422 --> 00:01:12,638
You're out shopping too?

11
00:01:12,905 --> 00:01:13,326
Yeah.

12
00:01:14,458 --> 00:01:15,605
Just picking up a few things.

13
00:01:18,319 --> 00:01:19,674
Oh, this is my daughter, Nava.

14
00:01:20,350 --> 00:01:20,755
Nava.

15
00:01:21,272 --> 00:01:22,285
Say hello to Dear.

16
00:01:24,777 --> 00:01:25,956
Hello, Nava.

17
00:01:27,332 --> 00:01:28,095
I'm Dear.

18
00:01:29,481 --> 00:01:30,548
Hello.

19
00:01:35,327 --> 00:01:36,837
So, are you going back to work tonight?

20
00:01:39,657 --> 00:01:41,759
Today marks the end of your 10-day period.

21
00:01:42,047 --> 00:01:43,311
You've done a wonderful job.

22
00:01:43,555 --> 00:01:45,726
You've been working so well at the store

23
00:01:45,832 --> 00:01:48,328
that I'd love for you to stay on long-term.

24
00:01:49,047 --> 00:01:50,061
But, well...

25
00:01:50,903 --> 00:01:53,266
Ultimately, it's your decision.

26
00:01:59,477 --> 00:02:00,330
If I quit,

27
00:02:01,434 --> 00:02:03,157
will Dear be able to manage here on her own?

28
00:02:04,179 --> 00:02:05,843
You don't need to worry about that.

29
00:02:06,611 --> 00:02:08,003
I've already hired new employees.

30
00:02:09,649 --> 00:02:10,491
New employees?

31
00:02:11,115 --> 00:02:11,947
That's right.

32
00:02:12,321 --> 00:02:13,094
I've hired new people.

33
00:02:13,760 --> 00:02:16,634
But having someone as experienced as you

34
00:02:16,997 --> 00:02:18,560
around to train them

35
00:02:19,480 --> 00:02:20,638
would be great.

36
00:02:24,895 --> 00:02:25,647
So, what do you say?

37
00:02:27,119 --> 00:02:28,068
Do you want to keep working?

38
00:02:32,527 --> 00:02:33,364
I don't think I'll be going.

39
00:02:40,979 --> 00:02:41,752
I understand.

40
00:02:45,046 --> 00:02:45,510
Dear.

41
00:02:47,668 --> 00:02:48,534
Take care of yourself.

42
00:02:53,125 --> 00:02:53,738
I'm off.

43
00:02:55,646 --> 00:02:56,638
Bye, Nava.

44
00:03:05,909 --> 00:03:06,912
Your shoes are ready.

45
00:03:13,463 --> 00:03:14,505
Do you want to put them on now?

46
00:03:18,204 --> 00:03:19,681
Mom, how are you doing?

47
00:03:20,474 --> 00:03:21,962
It's a nice day today.

48
00:03:23,500 --> 00:03:24,690
I brought you some oranges.

49
00:03:25,351 --> 00:03:27,495
I remember how much you love them.

50
00:03:32,794 --> 00:03:34,056
Remember when I used to study late at night

51
00:03:34,080 --> 00:03:35,631
for the police cadet exam?

52
00:03:38,449 --> 00:03:39,175
Back then,

53
00:03:40,225 --> 00:03:42,215
you always brought me oranges.

54
00:03:51,758 --> 00:03:52,153
Mom.

55
00:03:57,578 --> 00:03:58,175
Mom.

56
00:03:58,602 --> 00:03:59,332
Mom! Stop!

57
00:03:59,940 --> 00:04:00,308
Stop!

58
00:04:00,879 --> 00:04:01,503
Mom!

59
00:04:02,250 --> 00:04:02,692
Mom!

60
00:04:05,191 --> 00:04:06,167
Mom! Please stop!

61
00:04:08,807 --> 00:04:09,292
Mom!

62
00:04:09,753 --> 00:04:10,361
Mom!

63
00:04:15,209 --> 00:04:15,875
Nurse!

64
00:04:16,184 --> 00:04:16,952
Nurse!

65
00:04:21,815 --> 00:04:22,348
Mom!

66
00:04:22,753 --> 00:04:23,809
Please step back.

67
00:04:25,697 --> 00:04:26,316
Ma'am.

68
00:04:27,853 --> 00:04:28,626
Please calm down.

69
00:04:29,986 --> 00:04:30,946
Straighten your back.

70
00:04:34,413 --> 00:04:35,074
Straighten your back.

71
00:04:36,413 --> 00:04:37,320
Straighten your back.

72
00:04:39,431 --> 00:04:40,188
Straighten your back.

73
00:04:45,057 --> 00:04:45,702
Nava.

74
00:04:45,931 --> 00:04:46,657
Let's go.

75
00:06:05,286 --> 00:06:06,774
Two bowls of wonton noodle soup, please.

76
00:06:07,014 --> 00:06:08,262
Sure. Just a moment.

77
00:06:09,864 --> 00:06:11,411
Hello, Metha.

78
00:06:12,205 --> 00:06:13,971
It's been a while. How have you been?

79
00:06:17,496 --> 00:06:18,013
Hey.

80
00:06:19,655 --> 00:06:20,359
Hey, pretty lady.

81
00:06:20,383 --> 00:06:23,121
Your daughter gets cuter every day.

82
00:06:25,090 --> 00:06:26,605
May I have it?

83
00:06:26,629 --> 00:06:27,719
May I have a look?

84
00:06:29,884 --> 00:06:30,679
What do you want?

85
00:06:32,807 --> 00:06:33,159
Come on.

86
00:06:34,050 --> 00:06:36,919
You already know what I want.

87
00:06:39,785 --> 00:06:40,782
Give me another ten days.

88
00:06:41,742 --> 00:06:43,065
I'll get you another 100,000.

89
00:06:44,712 --> 00:06:46,659
10 days for 100,000?

90
00:06:49,014 --> 00:06:50,806
Where are you going to get that much money?

91
00:06:52,604 --> 00:06:53,740
I'll earn it.

92
00:06:55,514 --> 00:06:57,023
Don't lie to me.

93
00:06:57,460 --> 00:06:59,252
I've got my eye on you every day.

94
00:07:00,498 --> 00:07:02,295
I've seen you working at that convenience store.

95
00:07:02,844 --> 00:07:04,471
How are you going to come up with 100,000?

96
00:07:04,764 --> 00:07:05,687
I'm not lying.

97
00:07:06,499 --> 00:07:07,864
I earn 10,000 a day working there.

98
00:07:11,400 --> 00:07:11,688
Fine.

99
00:07:12,627 --> 00:07:13,715
I'll take your word for it.

100
00:07:14,734 --> 00:07:16,334
But do you know where that store

101
00:07:16,691 --> 00:07:17,454
gets its money from?

102
00:07:20,060 --> 00:07:21,260
I don't know. I've never asked.

103
00:07:21,612 --> 00:07:22,108
See?

104
00:07:22,994 --> 00:07:24,663
That's exactly your problem.

105
00:07:25,376 --> 00:07:27,275
That's why you can never pay off your debt.

106
00:07:27,718 --> 00:07:29,712
You're only interested in small sums.

107
00:07:32,807 --> 00:07:33,458
What are you going to do?

108
00:07:34,770 --> 00:07:36,167
Well, since you don't know,

109
00:07:36,852 --> 00:07:38,569
I have to ask someone who does, right?

110
00:07:40,436 --> 00:07:40,996
Don't.

111
00:07:41,736 --> 00:07:42,322
That place...

112
00:07:44,178 --> 00:07:44,968
What's wrong with that place?

113
00:07:51,722 --> 00:07:52,383
Why?

114
00:07:53,839 --> 00:07:54,559
It's dangerous.

115
00:08:01,782 --> 00:08:02,812
Are you worried about me?

116
00:08:03,852 --> 00:08:04,598
That's sweet.

117
00:08:05,673 --> 00:08:06,964
But now that you've said that,

118
00:08:07,526 --> 00:08:08,985
I'm even more curious.

119
00:08:14,321 --> 00:08:14,694
Hey.

120
00:08:15,675 --> 00:08:16,134
Yes, boss.

121
00:08:18,921 --> 00:08:20,169
See you, Nava.

122
00:08:23,970 --> 00:08:24,770
Are you okay, Nava?

123
00:08:40,187 --> 00:08:40,864
Who's that?

124
00:08:43,670 --> 00:08:44,758
Oh, Sugar.

125
00:08:47,088 --> 00:08:48,011
Why haven't you gone home yet?

126
00:08:48,475 --> 00:08:49,467
My shift's just started.

127
00:08:50,822 --> 00:08:51,057
Huh?

128
00:08:51,937 --> 00:08:52,545
What did you say?

129
00:08:52,875 --> 00:08:53,451
What do you mean

130
00:08:54,200 --> 00:08:54,872
your shift's just started?

131
00:08:55,683 --> 00:08:57,789
I'm working the night shift now.

132
00:08:58,083 --> 00:08:59,443
Today is my first day.

133
00:09:40,103 --> 00:09:42,044
May I invite Police Lieutenant General Nakarin

134
00:09:42,456 --> 00:09:43,100
to present

135
00:09:43,124 --> 00:09:45,537
the Outstanding Police Officer of the Year award

136
00:09:46,047 --> 00:09:48,767
to Special Police Colonel Wirat Trivikoon?

137
00:09:48,791 --> 00:09:49,822
Please come forward.

138
00:10:18,102 --> 00:10:19,174
Is this your son, Wirat?

139
00:10:20,073 --> 00:10:20,431
Yes.

140
00:10:21,286 --> 00:10:21,935
Metha.

141
00:10:22,521 --> 00:10:23,316
My only son.

142
00:10:23,497 --> 00:10:24,719
He's grown so much.

143
00:10:25,911 --> 00:10:28,340
I heard you're taking the police cadet exam this year.

144
00:10:29,556 --> 00:10:30,719
That's wonderful, Wirat.

145
00:10:30,980 --> 00:10:32,767
Your son is following in his father's footsteps.

146
00:10:33,207 --> 00:10:34,423
Well, good luck.

147
00:10:35,079 --> 00:10:36,801
With your father as a role model,

148
00:10:37,093 --> 00:10:38,192
make sure you study hard.

149
00:10:38,533 --> 00:10:40,487
Your family will be proud.

150
00:10:42,007 --> 00:10:42,777
Wirat, come here a moment.

151
00:10:42,840 --> 00:10:43,237
Yes, sir.

152
00:10:43,881 --> 00:10:45,625
How is the assignment I gave you coming along?

153
00:10:45,806 --> 00:10:47,001
Don't worry, sir.

154
00:10:47,660 --> 00:10:49,761
I've got the help of an expert

155
00:10:49,786 --> 00:10:51,683
to oversee this matter.

156
00:10:51,791 --> 00:10:54,602
The witnesses and evidence are now solid.

157
00:10:54,626 --> 00:10:56,858
I think we'll be able to close the case soon.

158
00:10:56,936 --> 00:10:57,482
I'm counting on you.

159
00:10:57,507 --> 00:10:57,951
Yes, sir.

160
00:10:58,866 --> 00:11:01,063
It took me quite a while to gather the evidence.

161
00:11:07,279 --> 00:11:07,844
Dad.

162
00:11:08,821 --> 00:11:09,338
Nava.

163
00:11:26,745 --> 00:11:27,623
Can't sleep, Nava?

164
00:11:39,782 --> 00:11:41,345
Shall I read you a story?

165
00:11:51,215 --> 00:11:52,186
Once upon a time,

166
00:11:53,087 --> 00:11:54,687
there was a young girl.

167
00:11:55,396 --> 00:11:56,830
She walked into the forest

168
00:11:58,200 --> 00:12:00,830
and found a little white rabbit.

169
00:12:05,756 --> 00:12:06,101
So...

170
00:12:06,652 --> 00:12:08,290
How did you end up working the night shift?

171
00:12:09,201 --> 00:12:09,825
Well...

172
00:12:10,030 --> 00:12:11,385
I saw

173
00:12:11,627 --> 00:12:13,537
the night-shift recruitment sign outside the store.

174
00:12:13,948 --> 00:12:15,857
Then I asked Cherd, and he said

175
00:12:15,943 --> 00:12:18,098
if I'd seen the sign, I could start work right away.

176
00:12:19,308 --> 00:12:19,986
No!

177
00:12:21,436 --> 00:12:22,066
Why not?

178
00:12:22,399 --> 00:12:25,471
Switch shifts right now, or tell Cherd you're quitting.

179
00:12:26,271 --> 00:12:27,321
Wait.

180
00:12:28,404 --> 00:12:29,860
Sugar, listen to me.

181
00:12:30,489 --> 00:12:32,409
The night shift isn't as easy as you think.

182
00:12:34,156 --> 00:12:34,881
Why not?

183
00:12:35,991 --> 00:12:37,521
I haven't even tried it yet.

184
00:12:37,708 --> 00:12:39,156
Besides, you won't be lonely anymore.

185
00:12:39,181 --> 00:12:40,469
I'll keep you company.

186
00:12:40,636 --> 00:12:41,905
No means no!

187
00:12:50,108 --> 00:12:50,673
Dear.

188
00:12:51,473 --> 00:12:52,097
That hurts.

189
00:13:07,515 --> 00:13:08,171
Everyone.

190
00:13:10,176 --> 00:13:10,571
Here.

191
00:13:11,861 --> 00:13:14,213
The newest members of our night-shift team.

192
00:13:19,761 --> 00:13:20,345
Cherd.

193
00:13:21,028 --> 00:13:22,532
You hired this many people?

194
00:13:23,087 --> 00:13:23,493
Oh.

195
00:13:24,053 --> 00:13:24,341
Well...

196
00:13:24,869 --> 00:13:26,351
We're short-staffed on the night shift.

197
00:13:29,111 --> 00:13:30,508
This looks pretty ordinary.

198
00:13:33,116 --> 00:13:34,108
All they do is stand at the register.

199
00:13:34,240 --> 00:13:35,723
Are they really paid 10,000 a day?

200
00:13:37,344 --> 00:13:39,248
If they are, I'm staying for good.

201
00:13:43,385 --> 00:13:45,201
I want everyone to work hard

202
00:13:45,226 --> 00:13:49,840
and follow all the rules for employees strictly.

203
00:13:51,819 --> 00:13:52,944
What rules?

204
00:13:54,355 --> 00:13:56,589
The 13 rules I told you about.

205
00:13:57,395 --> 00:14:00,536
The procedures for serving customers.

206
00:14:04,638 --> 00:14:06,499
And what if I don't want to follow them?

207
00:14:08,472 --> 00:14:10,413
I'd strongly advise you to.

208
00:14:11,938 --> 00:14:13,677
Because if you break a rule...

209
00:14:22,441 --> 00:14:24,377
It's time to start work, everyone.

210
00:14:25,534 --> 00:14:26,676
Welcome

211
00:14:27,328 --> 00:14:28,303
to the night shift.

212
00:16:39,219 --> 00:16:39,998
Was that the wind?

213
00:17:29,841 --> 00:17:30,551
What is this snack?

214
00:17:31,244 --> 00:17:32,551
It tastes awful.

215
00:17:34,567 --> 00:17:35,495
Try this flavor, boss.

216
00:17:36,078 --> 00:17:36,739
It's much better.

217
00:17:48,060 --> 00:17:49,159
Such stupid rules.

218
00:17:50,513 --> 00:17:51,009
So?

219
00:17:51,729 --> 00:17:52,449
Still tastes awful.

220
00:17:53,610 --> 00:17:55,249
You have to pay for store items before eating them.

221
00:18:02,150 --> 00:18:04,118
And what if I don't want to pay, darling?

222
00:18:04,619 --> 00:18:04,966
Huh?

223
00:18:06,187 --> 00:18:07,397
It's the store rule.

224
00:18:07,899 --> 00:18:08,469
Oh.

225
00:18:08,977 --> 00:18:09,611
Another rule.

226
00:18:10,357 --> 00:18:12,086
This place takes things way too seriously.

227
00:18:12,881 --> 00:18:15,291
Is it really that hard to pay before you eat?

228
00:18:17,998 --> 00:18:18,564
No.

229
00:18:19,838 --> 00:18:21,028
I just don't want to.

230
00:18:23,264 --> 00:18:24,400
Calm down, Dear. Just calm down.

231
00:18:33,270 --> 00:18:34,689
Hope he chokes to death.

232
00:18:47,242 --> 00:18:47,855
Boss.

233
00:18:49,076 --> 00:18:49,924
Water! Water!

234
00:18:50,159 --> 00:18:50,863
Yes, boss.

235
00:19:05,389 --> 00:19:05,997
Darn it!

236
00:19:10,882 --> 00:19:11,431
Water!

237
00:19:13,309 --> 00:19:14,109
Where's my water?

238
00:19:14,290 --> 00:19:14,877
Do you have it?

239
00:19:26,273 --> 00:19:27,220
Why do you look so pale?

240
00:19:29,785 --> 00:19:32,175
I thought I saw something.

241
00:19:35,144 --> 00:19:37,720
Hello. Welcome to Sunny Mart.

242
00:19:38,978 --> 00:19:40,781
Hello. Welcome to Sunny Mart.

243
00:19:59,530 --> 00:20:00,447
What is that, Dear?

244
00:20:03,420 --> 00:20:04,806
Same as usual for you, sir?

245
00:20:12,574 --> 00:20:13,150
Here you go.

246
00:20:23,267 --> 00:20:23,754
Lighter.

247
00:20:47,017 --> 00:20:47,501
Piak.

248
00:20:55,559 --> 00:20:56,108
Boss.

249
00:20:59,312 --> 00:20:59,888
You're dead.

250
00:21:49,516 --> 00:21:50,601
Pued!

251
00:22:06,293 --> 00:22:06,869
Don't.

252
00:22:07,127 --> 00:22:07,775
Don't.

253
00:22:08,111 --> 00:22:08,927
Don't!

254
00:22:09,603 --> 00:22:10,447
Don't come near me.

255
00:22:10,775 --> 00:22:11,345
Don't.

256
00:22:11,521 --> 00:22:12,252
Don't!

257
00:22:16,151 --> 00:22:17,105
Don't come near me.

258
00:22:19,116 --> 00:22:19,996
Get out!

259
00:22:20,492 --> 00:22:21,100
Don't!

260
00:22:21,244 --> 00:22:21,861
Get out!

261
00:22:25,119 --> 00:22:25,752
Sugar!

262
00:22:25,998 --> 00:22:26,723
Sugar!

263
00:22:27,022 --> 00:22:28,574
Sugar, turn around! Don't look!

264
00:22:28,599 --> 00:22:29,067
Sugar!

265
00:22:29,968 --> 00:22:30,939
Don't look. Turn around.

266
00:22:31,333 --> 00:22:32,096
Sugar, look at me.

267
00:22:32,278 --> 00:22:32,919
Look at me.

268
00:22:33,434 --> 00:22:34,223
Sugar, look at me.

269
00:22:35,047 --> 00:22:35,985
What is that thing, Dear?

270
00:22:36,498 --> 00:22:37,515
Stay here.

271
00:22:38,738 --> 00:22:40,397
I won't let it hurt you.

272
00:22:50,334 --> 00:22:51,880
Why did you kill me?

273
00:22:56,207 --> 00:22:58,181
I... I had no choice.

274
00:22:58,938 --> 00:23:00,266
You had!

275
00:23:00,511 --> 00:23:01,700
No!

276
00:23:01,903 --> 00:23:02,585
Don't!

277
00:23:02,928 --> 00:23:04,928
You had!

278
00:23:20,269 --> 00:23:20,930
So?

279
00:23:24,568 --> 00:23:25,112
Boss.

280
00:23:26,973 --> 00:23:27,602
Well...

281
00:23:30,615 --> 00:23:31,442
I...

282
00:23:32,782 --> 00:23:34,014
I don't want to collect debts anymore.

283
00:23:35,838 --> 00:23:36,366
I...

284
00:23:38,030 --> 00:23:39,017
Can I quit?

285
00:23:42,064 --> 00:23:42,992
You want to quit?

286
00:23:44,160 --> 00:23:44,741
Sure.

287
00:23:47,299 --> 00:23:48,499
I always give people a chance.

288
00:23:51,097 --> 00:23:51,913
Really, boss?

289
00:23:54,422 --> 00:23:55,264
Thank you.

290
00:23:58,688 --> 00:23:59,552
Give me a lighter.

291
00:24:01,676 --> 00:24:02,433
Oh, sure.

292
00:24:37,913 --> 00:24:39,151
It's out of gas, boss.

293
00:24:40,592 --> 00:24:41,604
I'll go buy you one.

294
00:24:41,726 --> 00:24:42,904
There's a shop nearby.

295
00:24:43,043 --> 00:24:44,115
Hurry back.

296
00:24:44,577 --> 00:24:45,038
Yes, boss.

297
00:25:02,717 --> 00:25:04,071
You really want to quit?

298
00:25:05,085 --> 00:25:05,501
Here.

299
00:25:06,373 --> 00:25:07,429
Here's your way out.

300
00:25:13,142 --> 00:25:14,828
Stop, don't!

301
00:25:26,892 --> 00:25:27,436
No!

302
00:25:27,735 --> 00:25:28,370
Don't!

303
00:25:30,000 --> 00:25:30,623
Piak.

304
00:25:30,975 --> 00:25:31,828
Don't come near me.

305
00:25:31,897 --> 00:25:32,271
Boss.

306
00:25:32,617 --> 00:25:33,065
It's me.

307
00:25:33,451 --> 00:25:34,214
Metha.

308
00:25:34,395 --> 00:25:35,158
Metha.

309
00:25:36,160 --> 00:25:37,227
It's going to kill me.

310
00:25:37,824 --> 00:25:38,299
Metha.

311
00:25:38,947 --> 00:25:39,757
The only way to survive

312
00:25:40,680 --> 00:25:41,523
is to follow the rules.

313
00:25:43,326 --> 00:25:44,574
What stupid rules?

314
00:26:01,986 --> 00:26:03,041
(Sweetheart)

315
00:26:09,236 --> 00:26:09,971
Rule number three.

316
00:26:10,072 --> 00:26:11,544
Employees must not use their mobile phones

317
00:26:11,568 --> 00:26:13,369
while on duty.

318
00:26:20,781 --> 00:26:21,501
Ped!

319
00:26:37,455 --> 00:26:38,275
No!

320
00:26:38,517 --> 00:26:39,142
No!

321
00:26:39,337 --> 00:26:40,384
Let me out!

322
00:26:40,501 --> 00:26:41,501
Let me out!

323
00:26:41,689 --> 00:26:42,619
Let me go!

324
00:26:42,832 --> 00:26:43,626
Let me go!

325
00:26:43,908 --> 00:26:44,486
No!

326
00:26:44,598 --> 00:26:45,942
Have you broken any of the rules?

327
00:26:47,030 --> 00:26:48,193
What stupid rules?

328
00:26:48,694 --> 00:26:49,963
Have you greeted the customer yet?

329
00:26:51,111 --> 00:26:52,514
What are you talking about?

330
00:26:52,823 --> 00:26:54,007
I don't know.

331
00:26:55,041 --> 00:26:55,767
Let me go!

332
00:26:56,991 --> 00:26:57,882
Ask the customer quickly

333
00:26:58,166 --> 00:26:59,387
if he needs anything else.

334
00:27:03,558 --> 00:27:04,058
Hurry!

335
00:27:07,043 --> 00:27:07,590
Piak.

336
00:27:09,012 --> 00:27:10,154
Piak, I'm sorry.

337
00:27:10,495 --> 00:27:10,996
Piak.

338
00:27:12,292 --> 00:27:13,316
Please don't kill me.

339
00:27:16,457 --> 00:27:17,075
Piak.

340
00:27:19,961 --> 00:27:21,065
No, Piak.

341
00:27:21,331 --> 00:27:21,758
No.

342
00:27:21,972 --> 00:27:23,481
Please don't kill me.

343
00:27:23,667 --> 00:27:24,243
Piak!

344
00:27:33,188 --> 00:27:34,158
No!

345
00:27:50,244 --> 00:27:52,372
Would you like anything else, sir?

346
00:27:55,661 --> 00:27:56,275
No, thank you.

347
00:28:10,933 --> 00:28:13,018
Thank you for shopping at Sunny Mart.

348
00:28:13,456 --> 00:28:14,853
Please come again.

349
00:28:17,548 --> 00:28:19,974
Thank you for shopping at Sunny Mart.

350
00:28:20,369 --> 00:28:21,729
Please come again.

351
00:29:33,411 --> 00:29:34,494
That was brutal.

352
00:29:37,797 --> 00:29:38,693
Next time,

353
00:29:39,370 --> 00:29:40,655
get a bigger bag.

354
00:29:45,617 --> 00:29:46,103
Cherd.

355
00:29:48,333 --> 00:29:50,125
How did you manage to hire those people?

356
00:29:55,315 --> 00:29:56,451
Why don't you tell me

357
00:29:57,347 --> 00:29:59,662
where you get the money from?

358
00:30:00,055 --> 00:30:01,137
What money?

359
00:30:03,767 --> 00:30:06,119
The night-shift employees' wages.

360
00:30:07,675 --> 00:30:09,597
The sign says they get 10,000 a day.

361
00:30:11,332 --> 00:30:14,105
You all saw the night-shift recruitment sign?

362
00:30:16,787 --> 00:30:18,051
Cut it out.

363
00:30:19,720 --> 00:30:20,920
Why are you paying them so much?

364
00:30:22,551 --> 00:30:24,444
And who's backing you?

365
00:30:28,118 --> 00:30:29,275
If you want to know,

366
00:30:30,017 --> 00:30:32,586
why don't you apply to join our night shift?

367
00:30:33,382 --> 00:30:34,753
Then all of you

368
00:30:35,788 --> 00:30:36,972
will find out everything.

369
00:30:38,811 --> 00:30:39,819
Did you plan this?

370
00:30:44,445 --> 00:30:46,648
Actually, no one who comes into this store

371
00:30:47,000 --> 00:30:48,493
is here by coincidence.

372
00:30:49,303 --> 00:30:52,202
Anyone who can see the night-shift recruitment sign

373
00:30:53,569 --> 00:30:54,865
must be someone

374
00:30:55,958 --> 00:30:57,089
who has a lot of karmic debt.

375
00:30:59,061 --> 00:30:59,674
A lot of karmic debt?

376
00:31:02,045 --> 00:31:02,856
What does that mean?

377
00:31:04,684 --> 00:31:06,033
Most of them...

378
00:31:08,582 --> 00:31:09,521
have taken someone's life.

379
00:31:15,434 --> 00:31:16,118
Sugar.

380
00:31:19,874 --> 00:31:20,866
What have you done?

381
00:31:47,682 --> 00:31:49,676
When will I finally die?

382
00:31:52,434 --> 00:31:53,687
I can't take this pain anymore.

383
00:31:54,972 --> 00:31:56,290
I can't go on.

384
00:31:57,890 --> 00:32:00,386
Please help me finally find peace.

385
00:32:02,089 --> 00:32:03,092
I can't do it.

386
00:32:04,356 --> 00:32:05,897
You take care of me every day.

387
00:32:07,006 --> 00:32:07,929
You know

388
00:32:08,707 --> 00:32:09,635
that living like this

389
00:32:10,700 --> 00:32:12,321
is just torture.

390
00:32:14,407 --> 00:32:16,119
Please do this for me.

391
00:32:18,007 --> 00:32:19,319
I'm begging you.

392
00:33:11,539 --> 00:33:13,017
I love you, Grandma.

393
00:33:21,458 --> 00:33:23,218
I didn't mean to.

394
00:33:26,846 --> 00:33:28,990
It was what Grandma wanted.

395
00:33:37,873 --> 00:33:38,668
Intentions

396
00:33:39,970 --> 00:33:41,452
don't matter as much as the outcome.

397
00:34:28,933 --> 00:34:29,621
Dear.

398
00:34:31,150 --> 00:34:31,726
Are you okay?

399
00:34:34,894 --> 00:34:35,390
I'm fine.

400
00:34:37,262 --> 00:34:37,642
But...

401
00:34:38,116 --> 00:34:39,652
What exactly is this place?

402
00:34:43,043 --> 00:34:43,939
You don't need to know.

403
00:34:45,315 --> 00:34:46,109
And from now on,

404
00:34:46,365 --> 00:34:48,008
don't work here anymore.

405
00:34:50,506 --> 00:34:51,279
Okay?

406
00:34:53,247 --> 00:34:53,551
Huh?

407
00:34:55,727 --> 00:34:56,532
Okay?

408
00:34:59,917 --> 00:35:00,277
Yes

409
00:35:04,062 --> 00:35:04,904
Because I...

410
00:35:05,971 --> 00:35:07,416
can't bear to lose anyone else.

411
00:35:09,829 --> 00:35:11,068
Especially you.

412
00:35:33,247 --> 00:35:33,748
Come on.

413
00:35:34,367 --> 00:35:35,034
Let's go home.

414
00:35:57,462 --> 00:35:58,235
You'll feel better.

415
00:36:00,197 --> 00:36:01,098
I'll pay for it.

416
00:36:01,903 --> 00:36:02,479
Thank you.

417
00:36:09,387 --> 00:36:10,619
And thank you so much

418
00:36:11,791 --> 00:36:12,767
for helping out last night.

419
00:36:14,463 --> 00:36:15,108
But...

420
00:36:15,983 --> 00:36:17,171
I can't pay you.

421
00:36:18,320 --> 00:36:20,171
You weren't on the night shift last night.

422
00:36:20,779 --> 00:36:22,208
I wasn't expecting to be paid.

423
00:36:22,859 --> 00:36:23,920
I was just worried, so I came.

424
00:36:27,150 --> 00:36:28,608
Who could've imagined that that would happen?

425
00:36:32,242 --> 00:36:32,935
At this store,

426
00:36:33,917 --> 00:36:35,319
anything can happen.

427
00:36:36,711 --> 00:36:37,089
For example,

428
00:36:38,407 --> 00:36:40,353
last night, we had so many employees.

429
00:36:41,407 --> 00:36:41,833
And now,

430
00:36:42,073 --> 00:36:43,423
we're short-staffed on the night shift again.

431
00:36:47,649 --> 00:36:48,065
Well...

432
00:36:49,686 --> 00:36:50,252
So...

433
00:36:51,366 --> 00:36:52,748
Are you coming back to work?

434
00:37:18,897 --> 00:37:19,627
Dad.

435
00:37:21,604 --> 00:37:22,283
Nava.

436
00:37:23,780 --> 00:37:24,322
You're up.

437
00:37:30,667 --> 00:37:31,510
Come on.

438
00:37:33,716 --> 00:37:34,253
Let's get you showered

439
00:37:35,156 --> 00:37:35,722
and ready for school.

440
00:38:16,578 --> 00:38:17,358
Fate.

441
00:38:18,344 --> 00:38:19,442
Fate

442
00:38:20,145 --> 00:38:21,798
must have brought us all together.

443
00:38:21,905 --> 00:38:23,611
You've lasted quite a while working here.

444
00:38:23,820 --> 00:38:24,831
Have you ever run into

445
00:38:24,856 --> 00:38:26,128
any of those customers outside the store?

446
00:38:26,726 --> 00:38:27,435
I don't know.

447
00:38:27,947 --> 00:38:28,827
But if I ever do,

448
00:38:29,004 --> 00:38:30,545
I'd rather meet them inside the store.

449
00:38:31,308 --> 00:38:32,428
Did you see something?

450
00:38:35,758 --> 00:38:36,270
Cherd.

451
00:38:36,622 --> 00:38:38,057
I've never seen this rule before.

452
00:38:42,724 --> 00:38:43,300
This is bad.

453
00:38:45,758 --> 00:38:46,550
The rules have changed.
